e/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-79339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-79339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-79339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R$ be a $8\\times 12$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(R))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $R.$ \n\nSince $R$ has $12$ columns and $8$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $R$ is \n\n$$\n12-8=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(R))=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-34900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-34904" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34904" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34904" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-34973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0+1+1=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-35316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-34902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n- If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\,0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.$\n- If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-139973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-34906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 12 & 7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))$, we reduce $Q$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 12 & 7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{5} & :={R}_{5}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $5$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-34914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-34914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(D)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(D)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D))$, we reduce $D$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(D)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D))=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 9 & 28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-7){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 23 & 56\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-35317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-35317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(W)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))$, we reduce $W$ to row echelon form, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and  $1$\n non-pivot column (the $2$nd). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433"} {"question" "q-139975" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139975" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "q-139975" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef2854a434979cbab911779753be3eb362d3eb5967a19581efb2e46e934074d7"} {"question" "e-5419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A$ is a $9 \\times 11$ matrix that has $9$ pivot columns, then what is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5419.json" "file_sha256" "011328f9089cd45396b8ee4cb71596812aeb592123bf4ed885085befbfd0dfb2"} {"question" "e-5419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A$. \n\nSince $A$ has $11$ columns and $9$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n11-9=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5419.json" "file_sha256" "011328f9089cd45396b8ee4cb71596812aeb592123bf4ed885085befbfd0dfb2"} {"question" "e-5421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/62cc7238e6676b8a43d216ab6c8b30504602c68fd548832eceac9b710b885471.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/b85d717afa8af39d10517f909a09b53e6d379beef6e04e3d9ce7d3e48c88dca4.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/8e12a5386c3db2149324bd28c174a5410f7751e0c963cf80969e0cfdf14e5d7b.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5421.json" "file_sha256" "6697ee091479547bd7fc8010eac92def0dad5eb754f0e38ceb518963c169859d"} {"question" "e-5421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5421.json" "file_sha256" "6697ee091479547bd7fc8010eac92def0dad5eb754f0e38ceb518963c169859d"} {"question" "e-5422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/e20df1b44d2bfe100499eebfb4d2bdf8c1055978fdccbe11c8b5c0882052ace8.png) what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5422.json" "file_sha256" "c0ac8852b651c33761e644728627a394d3cbae0cb0f757752086287688a2f9c1"} {"question" "e-5422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A)) = 1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5422.json" "file_sha256" "c0ac8852b651c33761e644728627a394d3cbae0cb0f757752086287688a2f9c1"}] "usage" {"q-35345" [] "q-34904" [] "e-5422" [] "q-34900" [] "q-79196" [] "e-5421" [] "e-5419" []} "basis" 2300 "retractions" [[17592186125141 :question/problem "If $A$ is a $5 \\cdot 8$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns, then $dim(Null(A)) =$"] [17592186124780 :question/problem "Let $R$ be a $8 \\cdot 12$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $R$?"] [17592186124781 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. If $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ then $dim(Null(A)) = 0$.\n2. If $B = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $dim(Null(B)) = 2$.\n3. If $C = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $dim(Null(C)) = 1$."] [17592186124792 :question/problem "If $D = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$, then $nullity(D) =$"] [17592186124235 :question/problem "If $A$ is a $9 \\times 11$ matrix that has $9$ pivot columns, then what is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$?"] [17592186124235 :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A$.\n\nSince $A$ has $11$ columns and $9$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is\n$11-9=2$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2\n$$\n\n."] [17592186124236 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. If $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n2. If $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n3. If $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$"] [17592186124236 :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix.\n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1$.\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=2$.\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$nd column). So, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."] [17592186124237 :question/problem "Given $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)$?"] [17592186124237 :question/worked-solution "To find $\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{3} &:=R_{3} + 3R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{4} \\mid:=R_{4} + 3R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column).\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A)) = 1\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186121703 17592186121704 17592186121705 17592186121706 17592186121707 17592186121709 17592186121710 17592186121711 17592186121712 17592186121713 17592186121775 17592186121776 17592186121777 17592186121778 17592186121779 17592186123869 17592186123870 17592186123871 17592186123872 17592186123873] "immutable_fields" [[17592186121702 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121702 :answer-field/id] [17592186121702 :answer-field/key] [17592186121702 :answer-field/type] [17592186121708 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121708 :answer-field/id] [17592186121708 :answer-field/key] [17592186121708 :answer-field/type] [17592186121774 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121774 :answer-field/id] [17592186121774 :answer-field/key] [17592186121774 :answer-field/type] [17592186123868 :answer-field/correct] [17592186123868 :answer-field/id] [17592186123868 :answer-field/key] [17592186123868 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
